    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "A persistent Mongoid model includes `Mongoid::Document`; typed fields can be declared with `field :name, type: String`. Instances can be stored in a collection or embedded in other documents. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/mongoid/current/data-modeling/documents.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:74d8f89cc1e5f445f46810a71edb4f3ee20c4c453d0c2a9cf71c6a2adc42a4e3",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:2256252bbe9806124be78006b50b7962d65bfdd944952087f5dc12f86781c268",
            "ev:9221f50f8647d0aa69447cdc1a9025db5310a863b15be236e680c766ecb053b2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Embedded associations use `embeds_one` or `embeds_many` on the parent and `embedded_in` on the child. The child is stored inside the parent; multiple children are stored as an array field. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/mongoid/current/data-modeling/associations/embedded-associations.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:7ebcd659c9fe4c825013d2a71994ee7f4d99d4eb227c9eeceadeea14cea5edf6",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0b2e00b685795eac9ca17e9419ccb893fd431ed9fc87c71d852ffe258e378fae",
            "ev:624a514e5eabcff58546f14a630e98b4c3648fc40e665537b459e7b56bed5103",
            "ev:ea69afe95bdfa28504f5b8e71a0a89ce08a688d6643b23905d11f830911a15ad",
            "ev:f3ee014e277f531ffcc3f17723fd1e5435a36945c52777cff3bf5539f89f0825"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/mongoid/current/data-modeling/documents.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Referenced associations support `has_one`, `has_many`, `belongs_to`, and `has_and_belongs_to_many`. By default, `belongs_to` stores the parent’s `_id` in the child document. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/mongoid/current/data-modeling/associations/referenced-associations.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:ea6045352f7a8f770ff4469c4d08b1276910a95838874117df033a8243aa0990",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:bf54094b6645d1c01b7dea576da9bad3849b8f78d81b14c213c03472dee517de",
            "ev:fdfd7584d5bbb5868acad731152905dab3329238eca8e86b55e790d937f7abb0"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Association callbacks `before_add`, `after_add`, `before_remove`, and `after_remove` apply to `embeds_many`, `has_many`, and `has_and_belongs_to_many`. Register them as association options and pass the added or removed document to the callback. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/mongoid/current/data-modeling/callbacks.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:a11e8d0ee00e40914a535e2a6b0b8d3caeeff6684c911cea75f2442ebb3654cb",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:ec4231e37689ec305c8519f2990f87e711115266a3f44ceddeb2dfdb47ee8bab"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Deletion paths have different callback semantics: document `delete` skips callbacks while `destroy` runs them; for embedded associations, `clear` and `delete_all` skip destroy callbacks while `destroy_all` runs them. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/mongoid/current/interact-data/crud.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:bbf776bb02ff78695b3479f38e6031f02b5d9800ec2f91aec6fa74c9f7b5ccdd",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0b0e32489c7bbbe3bda8d0b3156cce33e42ea8da3fed43d2c8e6fe6b71d14a0f",
            "ev:0ca89e880727781b6d3e3b272af20010eb77b32c6263a066e3e677d0c3189ec4",
            "ev:1e6aa7896f039e8cedf00423a71e6d5045507b5799b5b08aea043dc73a67a0de",
            "ev:357c86cb1a6725bc27ab8fdca22fd528cb69ce56091caaa3b61d3ce053193b40",
            "ev:d3a285601652b27730771a1b233218d2b290424742f24bc7b9e2a6aea1345af6"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/mongoid/current/data-modeling/associations/embedded-associations.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Mongoid query methods return chainable, lazily evaluated `Mongoid::Criteria` objects. Iterating results executes the query; chaining query methods merges filter criteria. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/mongoid/current/interact-data/specify-query.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:fafce5bd473dec8acd40f60c58dd0d09391528c161c1ddeb7046e79375388ad4",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:445288724c526c139835917817acb6b0c0f52273ea9a07876d666ad1d204b522",
            "ev:5e5993009c3df8ccde0f8176560e63545b50c617030d1baeb023ef1e15403ddd"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Embedded matching filters associations already loaded in the application without querying the server. Its supported operators are narrower than server queries: text, geospatial, JavaScript execution, `$expr`, and `$jsonSchema` are not implemented. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/mongoid/current/data-modeling/associations/embedded-associations.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:f3087eb437effb1d4cccdf19673cc2975e4aa5a8b9d4a188f43ef2f3c04d4181",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:941da230731efc9f660a80a63539ba44ebaeb0adfa389ccb4ff3be4513d36c15",
            "ev:f44df9f55e6e42518ac13a7c9da8b6722f99da39167b1928efb9f14028d5f3f2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A historical embedded-assignment performance investigation attributed increasing Ruby-side work to `object_already_related?`; Alex Bevilacqua profiled the issue without a database connection. This supports profiling association construction separately from database operations, not an unconditional claim that current releases retain the defect. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/MONGOID-4889",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:fdb9aa4ef4f1461e148c9a4f059e7ae7afe329129f3493e4d82ff2b67095c762",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:22093c5df0733d5cea9e950ddfa2f1799f48c8bfbbedbf14dbaef86e925363cc",
